  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0113" xml:lang="en">
        <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00383/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
          <div>
            <ab hand="#hand_gray_oegfl">
              <lb/>A2
              <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Auden</rs>
            </ab>
          </div>
          <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_cc_bronold">
            <opener>
              <dateline>
                <date>
                  <lb/><space quantity="29" unit="char"/>October 1st, l973.
                </date>
              </dateline>
              <salute>
                <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_4">Mr. Kallman</rs>,
              </salute>
            </opener>
            <p>
              <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_137">Dr. Kraus</rs> being absent from <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_1">Vienna</rs> the sad task
              <lb/>falls upon me to express our sincerest sympathies to you.
              <lb/>It would be vain to try an<add hand="#hand_blue_bronold" place="inline">d</add> find words of comfort, all we
              <lb/>can do is say that we fe<subst><del rend="erased" hand="#type_cc_bronold">l</del><add hand="#type_cc_bronold" place="superimposed">e</add></subst>l with you.
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>I just want to add that the <rs type="event" ref="#amp_event_id_3">lecture</rs> on Friday went
              <lb/>very well indeed. <space quantity="1" unit="char"/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr. Auden</rs> seemed to enjoy himself, and
              <lb/>the public responded enthusiastically. <space quantity="1" unit="char"/>He closed with the
              <lb/><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_312" ana="#ana_109">two funny four-liners</rs> on <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_11">Goethe</rs> and <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_319">Kant</rs>, and the applause
              <lb/>turned into a delighted ovation. <space quantity="1" unit="char"/>In our sorrow we are
              <lb/>glad to think that there was a l<subst><del rend="erased" hand="#type_cc_bronold">l</del><add hand="#type_cc_bronold" place="superimposed">a</add></subst>st occasion where people
              <lb/>could show him how deeply they appreciated his art, but
              <lb/>also how fond they were of him.
            </p>
            <closer>
              <salute>
                <lb/><space quantity="28" unit="char"/><subst><del rend="erased" hand="#type_cc_bronold"><unclear>C</unclear></del><add hand="#type_cc_bronold" place="superimposed">S</add></subst>incerely yours,
              </salute>
              <signed>
                <lb/><space quantity="27" unit="char"/>(<rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_135">Hella Bronold</rs>)
              </signed>
            </closer>
          </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00384/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
